        "body": "### How to reproduce this bug?\n\n\n```bash\n# Setup\ndocker run -d --name weaviate-test \\\n  -e AUTHENTICATION_ANONYMOUS_ACCESS_ENABLED=true \\\n  -e PERSISTENCE_DATA_PATH=/var/lib/weaviate \\\n  -p 8080:8080 \\\n  semitechnologies/weaviate:1.38.0\n\nsleep 15\n\n# Test case 1: desiredCount=0 IS rejected (control)\ncurl -s -o /dev/null -w \"%{http_code}\" -X POST http://localhost:8080/v1/schema \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"class\":\"TestZero\",\"shardingConfig\":{\"desiredCount\":0}}'\n# Returns: 422\n\n# Test case 2: desiredCount=-1 is NOT rejected (the bug)\ncurl -s -o /dev/null -w \"%{http_code}\" -X POST http://localhost:8080/v1/schema \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"class\":\"TestNeg\",\"shardingConfig\":{\"desiredCount\":-1}}'\n# Returns: 200 (bug!)\n\n# Cleanup\ndocker rm -f weaviate-test\n```\n\n### What is the expected behavior?\n\nWeaviate should reject ALL non-positive `desiredCount` values consistently. A shard count must be a positive integer (>=1). Weaviate already validates `desiredCount=0` and rejects it with 422, proving this field is validated. The same validation should reject `-1`, `-100`, and any other non-positive value.\n\n### What is the actual behavior?\n\n\nWeaviate inconsistently accepts `desiredCount=-1` (returns 200 and creates the schema) while rejecting `desiredCount=0` (returns 422). Both values are equally invalid for a shard count, but only one is rejected. A negative shard count is logically impossible and leads to undefined behavior during vector indexing.\n\n\n### Supporting information\n\n\n**Evidence of inconsistency:**\n- Weaviate rejects `desiredCount=0` with 422, proving it validates this field for non-positive values\n- But Weaviate accepts `desiredCount=-1` with 200, even though `-1` is equally non-positive\n- This inconsistent validation suggests the bounds check only tests `value > 0` in some code paths but uses `value == 0` (or `value >= 0`) in others, missing the negative range\n\n\n### Server Version\n\n1.38.0\n\n### Weaviate Setup\n\nSingle Node\n\n### Nodes count\n\n1\n\n### Code of Conduct\n\n- [x] I have read and agree to the Weaviate's [Contributor Guide](https://weaviate.io/developers/contributor-guide) and [Code of Conduct](https://weaviate.io/service/code-of-conduct)",
